From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexandre Derumier <aderumier@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:35:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] qasf: Deliver each output on its own thread.

Patch 0017 turned DedicatedDeliveryThread off, delivering every output
from the WM async reader's callback thread. That thread also requests
each stream's next read after delivering its sample: an audio renderer
blocking in Receive() until its samples are due then holds back the
video behind each audio sample (about 25 frames per second for a 60 fps
stream with 42 ms audio packets), the video falls behind the stream time
and a renderer dropping late frames shows none.

Deliver each output on its own thread again, as Windows and upstream
Wine do. Delivering only the audio on its own thread was not enough:
the video, still paced on the callback thread, ended up 0.6 s late.

Game impacted: Hatsune Miku Project DIVA Arcade (Sega RingEdge 2): its
WMV3 1280x720 60 fps attract movie stayed on its first frames (or froze
midway) with its sound playing. Its DirectShow renderers are its own:
the audio one blocks for each sample's duration, the video one drops the
frames whose time has passed. With this patch the whole movie plays, its
video 0.16 s ahead of the stream time.

Also tested with Deadly Premonition (Director's Cut, GOG), the game patch
0017 was written for (its VC-1 WMV movies through the WM ASF Reader into
a Sample Grabber): with DedicatedDeliveryThread back to TRUE (and the next
patch), its movies play fine, no regression.
---
--- a/dlls/qasf/asfreader.c
+++ b/dlls/qasf/asfreader.c
@@ -604,10 +604,10 @@
             break;
         }
 
-        /* WMReader already paces async samples. Deliver qasf outputs from the
-         * callback thread so audio and video callbacks stay in timestamp order
-         * instead of drifting on separate delivery threads. */
-        value = FALSE;
+        /* Deliver each output on its own thread, as Windows does: a renderer
+         * blocking in Receive() until its samples are due (audio ones) must
+         * not hold back the other outputs' samples. */
+        value = TRUE;
         if (FAILED(hr = IWMReaderAdvanced2_SetOutputSetting(reader_advanced, i, L"DedicatedDeliveryThread",
                 WMT_TYPE_BOOL, (BYTE *)&value, sizeof(value))))
         {
